# GGUF model-tooling Python dependencies.
# SINGLE source of truth: compile to requirements.txt via the pip-compile
# container in this dir (nerdctl build + run). Never hand-edit requirements.txt.
#
#   make generate-requirements
#
# Then install into the runtime venv:
#   make venv-install
numpy==2.4.6
gguf==0.19.0
# The `hf` (huggingface_hub) CLI is the official HF downloader used by
# `--download-top-tier`, scripts/hf_download.py, and download_test_model.py.
# Installing it into the venv makes the launcher self-contained so top-tier
# download works on any fresh machine regardless of what's in ~/models.
huggingface_hub[cli]==1.30.0
# The versions the daily security scan (issue #754) reports as the MINIMUM that clears an advisory.
# They reach requirements.txt transitively, so the resolver — not this file — used to decide them.
# Stating the report's own `fixed` value here makes pip-compile compile at or above it, and makes a
# version change a reviewed diff instead of a resolver side effect.
certifi>=2026.10.18   # GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 (critical) — trust store under every HF download
filelock>=4.2.1       # CVE-2026-112940 (high) — via huggingface-hub
urllib3>=2.8.0        # CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97689 (high) — via requests/gguf
# The security floors: the MINIMUM version every advisory the daily scan reports demands, written by
# `make security-bumps` (scripts/security_bumps.py, issue #738) and honoured here as constraints so
# the compiled requirements.txt is regenerated rather than hand-edited.
-c security-floors.in
